        "id": "correctness-average-div-zero-overflow",
        "title": "average() panics on empty slice and can overflow on sum",
        "lens": "correctness",
        "anchor": {
          "path": "reasoning-correctness/planted/correctness.rs",
          "line": 3,
          "text": "(total / values.len() as u64)"
        },
        "severity": "medium",
        "confidence": "confirmed",
        "evidence": [
          "reasoning-correctness/planted/correctness.rs:2",
          "reasoning-correctness/planted/correctness.rs:3",
          "reasoning-correctness/clean/correctness.rs:2-3"
        ],
        "failureScenario": "average(&[]) evaluates total / 0 and panics with 'attempt to divide by zero'. Separately, values.iter().sum() on u64 panics in debug builds and wraps silently in release builds when the total exceeds u64::MAX, so a large input gives a wrong average. The sibling clean version returns Option<u64> and uses try_fold with checked_add. The planted signature returns plain u64, so callers cannot tell these cases apart.",
        "action": "Return Option<u64>. Return None for an empty slice. Accumulate with checked_add (or u128), as the clean variant does.",
        "verifyStatus": "verified",
        "verificationMethod": "adversarial-skeptic-pass",
        "reviewAxis": "spec",
        "sourceQuote": "let total: u64 = values.iter().sum();\n    (total / values.len() as u64)",
        "sourceLocation": "reasoning-correctness/planted/correctness.rs:2-3",
        "disposition": "wrong",
        "changeAttribution": {
          "status": "unknown",
          "reason": "The snapshot has no git baseline (baseline status not-applicable). The planted/clean directories are sibling variants, not a base/head diff.",
          "baselineEvidence": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "correctness-clean-safepath-sync-throw",
        "title": "safePath throws synchronously for missing or escaping paths, bypassing the 404 handling",
        "lens": "correctness",
        "anchor": {
          "path": "legacy-security-adjudication/clean/src/handler.js",
          "line": 10,
          "text": "fs.readFile(safePath(req.query.path), \"utf8\", (error, data) => {"
        },
        "severity": "low",
        "confidence": "likely",
        "evidence": [
          "legacy-security-adjudication/clean/src/handler.js:5",
          "legacy-security-adjudication/clean/src/handler.js:6",
          "legacy-security-adjudication/clean/src/handler.js:10",
          "legacy-security-variant-analysis/clean/src/config-export.js:4"
        ],
        "failureScenario": "fs.realpathSync throws ENOENT for a nonexistent file. safePath also throws 'path escapes root'. Both throws happen synchronously inside the route handler, before the readFile callback that maps errors to 404. Under Express's default error handling a request for a missing file or a traversal attempt likely gets a 500 (with a stack trace unless NODE_ENV=production) instead of the intended 404. The same pattern is in config-export.js. I did not run it, and the Express version is not supplied.",
        "action": "Wrap safePath in try/catch inside the handlers and respond 404 (or 400 for escapes).",
        "verifyStatus": "unverified",
        "changeAttribution": {
          "status": "unknown",
          "reason": "No baseline is available.",
          "baselineEvidence": []
        }
      }
    ],
    "withdrawn": [],
